Context: notes on the 'structure at infinity' of the moduli spaces M_{g,ν}, the boundary of the Deligne–Mumford compactification viewed as a normal-crossings divisor D = ∪ D_α. On the previous page Grothendieck works with the normalized strata. D_α is a (normalized) codim-d stratum, D_{α,δ} is the space of 'incidences' between strata, and there are 'bord' maps D_{α,δ} → D_δ and 'normal' maps D_{α,δ} → D_α. (165) gives D_{α,α'} ×_{D_{α'}} D_{α',α''} ≅ D_{α,α',α''}, and (166) gives the projections from it. The direct map (167) D_{α,α',α''} → D_{α,α''} is not immediately visible, but (168) D_{α,α''} → D_α × D_{α''} exists.

This page, first part: (168) is a monomorphism. Hence (167) is uniquely determined by requiring compatibility with (168), using the two maps D_{α,α',α''} ⇉ D_α, D_{α''} already available from (166). This amounts to defining 'composition of incidences' by a mono-into-product argument. A marginal note says this works in the analytic context.

Second part: an abstract definition is introduced, a 'structure de déploiement (?) à l'infini … modulaire', first in the analytic setting. A marginal remark proposes a name for it. Its first layer is an internal category 𝒟 in the category of analytic spaces:
- D_*, the space of objects;
- D_{**}, the space of arrows;
- source and target ('but') maps s, b: D_{**} → D_*;
- an identity map D_* → D_{**};
- composition (D_{**}, b) ×_{D_*} (D_{**}, s) → D_{**}, (u, v) ↦ v∘u;
- the usual associativity and unit axioms, i.e. for every S the S-valued points form a category.

The next page adds a codimension function c: D_* → ℕ, giving D_* = ∐ D_d and D_{**} = ∐ D_{d,d'}. Arrows go only from higher to lower or equal codimension. Arrows between objects of equal codimension are identities. So 𝒟 is a 'directed' (Reedy-like, graded) internal category: the analytic 'category of strata' of the boundary. Objects are points of normalized strata; arrows are specializations, i.e. a point of a deeper stratum together with a branch of a shallower stratum through it. The aim is to axiomatize the combinatorial-analytic structure at infinity of M̄_{g,ν}, including how strata are glued along each other, as a single category object.
